You can drum with your doggy, drum with your chum, bitty.

00:43:00.060 --> 00:43:05.220
With your daddy, with your mom, with your doggy, with your chum

00:43:05.220 --> 00:43:07.480
Rum-tum-tum, everybody drum

00:43:07.480 --> 00:43:12.150
Drum-tum, everybody drum

00:43:12.150 --> 00:43:15.210
Drum-tum, everybody drum

00:43:16.000 --> 00:43:17.620
Rum-tum-tum-tum-tum

00:43:23.980 --> 00:43:26.460
Next on the Drum Channel, Endless Drummer

00:43:26.460 --> 00:43:28.120
Followed by Drumbo

00:43:32.680 --> 00:43:36.190
No, Elmo, it is ready!

00:43:36.470 --> 00:43:36.930
Ready?

00:43:38.480 --> 00:43:38.800
Whoa!

00:43:40.200 --> 00:43:42.000
It's been happening all day, Baby Bear.

00:43:42.160 --> 00:43:43.020
What's ready?

00:43:43.200 --> 00:43:48.180
Oh, I made the empty porridge container into a drum.

00:43:49.780 --> 00:43:51.920
You can make your own drum?

00:43:52.280 --> 00:43:55.690
Yeah, yeah, and you can also play your own drum, too.

00:43:56.130 --> 00:43:56.570
Oh.

00:44:00.240 --> 00:44:02.350
Dig that queasy sound!

00:44:02.370 --> 00:44:03.400
Yeah, dig!

00:44:05.150 --> 00:44:06.610
Drumming baby bear!

00:44:07.210 --> 00:44:10.460
Boy, can't wait to get some porridge!

00:44:10.780 --> 00:44:13.650
But first, Elmo wants to keep learning about drums!

00:44:15.210 --> 00:44:15.930
What could that be?

00:44:17.240 --> 00:44:17.460
Hey!

00:44:19.700 --> 00:44:22.380
Wanna talk to some bongo drums?

00:44:22.740 --> 00:44:26.070
Yeah! Beat drums, bongos!

00:44:26.790 --> 00:44:27.630
Beats me!

00:44:28.930 --> 00:44:29.970
That's a good one!

00:44:31.020 --> 00:44:33.960
Well, tell how much it sounds, bongos.

00:44:34.240 --> 00:44:37.080
OK, well, we're a musical instrument

00:44:37.080 --> 00:44:40.040
that you play with your hands.

00:44:40.600 --> 00:44:43.760
And we each have a different sound.

00:44:43.900 --> 00:44:45.340
Oh, oh, try it.

00:44:45.440 --> 00:44:46.660
Yeah, man, yeah.

00:44:50.550 --> 00:44:51.670
Now try me, man.

00:44:55.030 --> 00:44:55.830
Different sounds.

00:44:56.010 --> 00:44:56.790
Yeah, it is different.

00:44:57.030 --> 00:44:58.490
And you can play it softly.

00:44:58.710 --> 00:44:59.090
OK, sorry.

00:45:02.110 --> 00:45:04.140
Or loud.

00:45:09.500 --> 00:45:11.900
You can play us slowly, too.

00:45:12.260 --> 00:45:12.560
Slowly?

00:45:12.860 --> 00:45:12.960
Yeah.

00:45:21.960 --> 00:45:23.140
Daddy, let's go.

00:45:28.980 --> 00:45:29.960
You can play...

00:45:30.000 --> 00:45:32.160
all kinds of different music

00:45:32.160 --> 00:45:34.240
on all kinds of different drums.

00:45:34.720 --> 00:45:35.140
Really?

00:45:36.460 --> 00:45:38.620
Well, you can play Caribbean music

00:45:38.620 --> 00:45:40.400
on the steel drum.

00:46:04.830 --> 00:46:26.390
He loves drums.

00:46:26.670 --> 00:46:29.600
Sorry, that's just a sip.

00:46:37.800 --> 00:46:42.100
Oh well, that's why Dorothy wants us to sing the drum song!

00:46:49.200 --> 00:46:50.100
I love that song!

00:46:50.280 --> 00:46:51.280
Can we sing along?

00:46:51.520 --> 00:46:51.740
Sure!

00:46:53.020 --> 00:46:57.040
Drums, Drums, Drums, Drums, Drums, Drums, Drums, Drums, Drums, Drums!

00:46:57.040 --> 00:46:57.900
Oh, you sing along!

00:46:59.050 --> 00:46:59.970
Drums, Drums, Drums!

